{"kind":"assert","text":"Phase-2 coverage at main 86179b0c, as requested by 63d906c0. This is source inspection only. No compiler, test, regeneration, browser or gate ran for this report.\n\nPlan 035 delivered an internal program for admitted definitions: M1–M2 at 8b063123, clock metadata at e50d9eeb, guards and lists at 8d9080f3, effects at f04ff0f2, sends at 5a0e5660, Native and capability capture at 01de2ca8, and the complete body runner at 0914c89e. Current program/body.ts, interpret.ts and requirements.ts execute, explain and describe dependencies of the actual admitted body. They do not author definition data, derive client expected revisions, describe MCP tools, infer application manifests or generate stories. None of the six phase-2 requests is complete because of plan 035.\n\nCoverage and remaining work:\n\n1. DX-T0 6f87a4e3. Plan 035 delivered no requested consolidation. MCP shape.ts:189 still owns expectedOf and its prototype-safe subject resolution. CLI browser-helpers.ts:41 has another copy, and Counter browser/model.ts:141 derives revisions inline. Lending browser/model.ts:145, lending/test-support.ts and grow/test-support.ts still supply revisions by hand. application-scenarios.ts:103 resolves authored $revision references. MCP describe.ts still owns the five description derivations and imports local marks.ts. Its totality witness remains in mcp/test/describe.test.ts. CLI describe is another derivation. Remain: one portable expected implementation, one shared description implementation, their existing consumers, the reason for each deliberate test/scenario revision literal, and definition-derived browser models after T1. Regenerated lanes-reference and mcp-tools bytes, the Lending catalogue and both browser scenarios remain required evidence.\n\n2. DX-T1 00c50371. The admitted execution boundary at 0914c89e runs data through the existing validator. Plan 035 supplies no packages/define package. DX-TR, which predates 035, already put the revised authoring witness on main in e3cd24a8: spikes/typed-surface/lib.ts has the vocabulary, sibling references, grants/reasons, inline-rule hoisting, typed elements, compile diagnostics and normalization. These are design sources, not the requested supported package. Remain: promote and reconcile that surface as @generalbusiness/dap-define under normal strict options, preserve the four forms, keep compile refusal metadata outside canonical data as the readability note requires, add the package's own type/runtime checks, and prove exact current Lending, Counter commitments and Grow-site pins. Grow-room and change-lane witnesses stay canonical-only until K-spell. The existing spike assertions are not proof that today's changed production pins still match. Keep the JSON and add regeneration enforcement and the requested application-writing documentation. The old request's sentence that spikes were not landed is historical: both current and before-readability spike directories now exist on main.\n\n3. DX-T2 d5fa31c9. Plan 035 supplies admitted rule evaluation, not a typed author expression template or client API. The existing declaredHandle is earlier client work: 07f25df9 already has the current typed interface family, and current declared.ts:171 still signs caller-supplied expected or {}. It exposes a generic typed intent method, not the requested per-act methods. Remain: typed methods using T0's shared revision derivation, shared formFor/actsOn/card-slot derivations, the restricted-JSONata tagged template with typed field/slot interpolation, the real-scope Lending scenario and unchanged Lending catalogue. Do not expose program AST constructors as the authoring API.\n\n4. K-spell 2ad35350. Plan 035 preserved admitted bytes and their meaning. Its owned internal metadata does not normalize definition identity. The authoring spike's normalize is still outside kernel admission. Remain: the kernel decision under docs/kernel.md section7, compatibility with existing recorded definitions