tion note and evidence manifest.\n\nA. T0 revisions. New packages/client/src/expected.ts and packages/client/test/expected.test.ts; client/src/index.ts; mcp/src/shape.ts and test/shape.test.ts; cli/src/browser-helpers.ts and test/browser-boundary.test.ts; apps/counter/browser/model.ts and client.test.ts; examples/lending/test-support.ts and examples/grow/test-support.ts if their revisions become derived. Keep scenario JSON and its $revision resolver when they intentionally specify a replay fixture, with the required reason. CLI browser-helpers is sealed, so this head also owns scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs. The first spike's absent room.ts is not a new production consumer; T2 replaces its role.\n\nB. T0 descriptions. New client/src/describe.ts, client/src/mark-descriptions.ts and client/test/describe.test.ts; client/src/index.ts; mcp/src/describe.ts, src/marks.ts and test/describe.test.ts; cli/src/browser-helpers.ts and test/browser-boundary.test.ts; scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs. Preserve existing MCP exports through forwards where needed. Move the pure totality cases and retain MCP integration cases at their current boundary. Verify docs/lanes-reference.md and docs/mcp-tools.json unchanged rather than accepting rewritten output. A and B share files and run sequentially.\n\nC. T1 authoring. New packages/define package, source, tests and normal configs; package-lock.json; vitest.projects.mjs; scripts/test.mjs and gate.sh only for the new package/regeneration check; a new scripts/check-definition-pins.mjs; examples/lending/definition.ts, apps/counter/commitments.ts and new package test witnesses for Grow-site, Grow-room and the change lane; docs/write-an-application.md. Keep current pinned JSON unchanged. Reuse the settled spike surface, then retire its active product role without rewriting the preserved before-readability record.\n\nD. T0 browser types, after C. apps/counter/browser/model.ts, client.test.ts and a new annotations.ts; examples/lending/browser/model.ts, model.test.ts and a new annotations.ts. Derive model act/field/limit types from the exported authored values and keep refusal annotations outside the pin. No client API or authoring-package edit belongs in D. The native and browser acceptance runs still have their normal slot requirements.\n\nE. T2 client and expressions, after T0 and C. client/src/declared.ts, index.ts, new forms.ts and their client tests; new define/src/expression.ts and its type tests plus define/src/index.ts; mcp/src/catalogue.ts and its catalogue support test; cli/src/browser-helpers.ts, test/browser-boundary.test.ts and scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs; new scope/test/typed-lending.test.ts. Reuse B's description derivation. Keep application browser models owned by D rather than editing them here.\n\nF. K-spell, after E and the migration ruling. derive/src/validate/canonical-spelling.ts plus the format dispatcher/admission call and definition-format test; examples/grow/room.ts, Grow's component form sources and pin-reference consumers; lanes/src/change.ts, shared.ts, digests.ts, definitions/change.json and the lane pin/reference generator outputs; docs/kernel.md only if the approved rule requires text, plus the migration note. The Grow-site dependency above prevents a final disjoint-path claim for F today. Preserve all recorded old-pin meaning. Planner owns live room selection, deployment and activation.\n\nG. T3 exact definitions and remaining forms, after E and F. define/src/index.ts, builder modules and builder tests; examples/grow/room.ts, site.ts and component form sources; lanes/src/change.ts, issue.ts and shared.ts; docs/write-an-application.md. Regeneration compares with the already migrated pins. It does not introduce another pin migration.\n\nH. T4 manifests, stories and typed views, after G. New define/src/manifest.ts, story.ts, views.ts, provenance.ts, their tests and define/src/index.ts; examples/lending/dap.application.json and scenarios/application.json as unchanged-output witnesses with authored sibling builder sources; apps/counter/dap.application.json and authored sibling manifest source; examples/lending/browser/projection.ts and apps/counter/browser/projection.ts for typed view declarations; cli/src/application-scenarios.ts only if accepting the typed-story output needs an adapter; docs/write-an-application.md. Keep binding and scenario formatv1 unchanged.\n\nWith those proposed boundaries, path-disjoint source-preparation pairs are A–C, A–G, A–H, B–C, B–D, B–G, B–H, C–D, D–E, D–G and D–H. Their dependency order still governs validation and landing. No F pair is claimed until its migration frontier is fixed. All other pairs share a named path, notably client exports, define exports, the browser model or the writing guide. Any newly discovered shared config or generated owner requires the heads to merge in sequence.\n\nA, B and E also share scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs with R3a/R3b. BR13's outside-catalog inventory may share that seal table and runtime consumers with these heads. Do not schedule them as path-independent merely because their main modules differ. C's new authoring package can prepare beside A or B without touching those sealed owners, subject to your placement. One local executable validation body and one gate remain the machine-wide rule.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true"}}